      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 222: 🔴 `CirclePolicy::isValid()` only checks identifiers for emptiness (e.g., member URI/role/channel IDs) while the record parser enforces strict formats. This allows malformed IDs to enter policy snapshots when `CirclePolicy` is built or mutated through non-record code paths, creating inconsistent behavior between in-memory policy evaluation and record-based validation. Add shared identifier validators (same constraints as record parsing) and enforce them in `isValid()` plus mutation paths (`SetCircleRole`, `InviteCircleMember`, `RegisterCircleChannel`, etc.) to keep invariants uniform.",
      "revId": "30abb2314af1254270313277efaee1bad8c422da",
